meta {
  name: 07 - Android First Chat Visual Counterpart
  seq: 8
}

docs {
  Use this folder to simulate the other participant while the Android emulator drives the real/current Firebase user.
  
  Assumptions:
  - Backend is running with local-firebase.
  - Bruno environment has firebase_api_key.
  - Android user already has an ACTIVE compatible profile and is queued from the app.
  - Optional but recommended: set androidUserId to the backend UUID returned by GET /api/me in the app/user flow.
  
  Typical flow:
  1. Android app enters matchmaking room and calls POST /api/matchmaking/queue.
  2. Run 00-12 in this folder to create/provision/enqueue a Firebase counterpart and process matchmaking. Use 03 only if you also want Bruno to refresh the Android/current-user Firebase token. Requests 09a-09c cover Firebase email verification: 09b must fail with EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED, then open the verification email, rerun 09c to refresh the token, and continue with 10.
  3. Android app polls GET /api/me/home and should see a FIRST_CHAT item in pendingActions[].
  4. Run 13-19 to make the counterpart enter first chat, send a message, advance first-chat guidance with Android, optionally send one counterpart audio message, approve first chat, optionally run 17a to make delayed visual review appear in Home immediately, and approve visual review.
  5. Scheduling scenario A: after Android and counterpart approve visual, run 22a then 22 to make scheduling available, then run 23-25 to inspect the connection, negotiation and proposals.
  6. Scheduling scenario B: Android sends slots from the app, then run 26b to submit counterpart slots with an overlap and auto-confirm the negotiation.
  7. Scheduling scenario C: Android sends slots from the app, then run 26c to submit counterpart slots without overlap, run 29 to reject only Android's pending partner proposals, then refresh with 24 and 25. A single rejection may keep the same round open.
  8. Scheduling scenario D: Android sends slots from the app, run 25 to capture proposalAId, then run 28 to accept that Android proposal from the counterpart.

  Scheduling date variables:
  - Set secondChatDateTime to the Android-proposed instant when testing overlap or manual acceptance.
  - Set counterpartSecondChatDateTime/counterpartSecondChatDateTimeLater to future half-hour aligned instants for the generic counterpart submit request.
  - Set counterpartNoOverlapDateTime/counterpartNoOverlapDateTimeLater to future half-hour aligned instants that do not overlap Android.
  - If any example dates are in the past, update them before sending proposals.
  
  This folder creates a fresh Firebase Auth user on every setup run using firebase_counterpart_email and firebase_counterpart_password environment variables generated by 00 Setup.
  Firebase id tokens and UIDs returned by sign-in are stored as Bruno runtime variables with the same names used in headers. Do not persist them in local.bru; rerun the sign-in request to refresh them.
}
